  "_note": "Any other expenditure, not capital, laid out wholly and exclusively for making or earning the income is deducted (D-194; rulebook OS-GENERAL-001) — but never personal expenses, nor interest or salary payable outside India untaxed (OS-NODED-001: a nil line), nor anything against dividends or unit income (OS-DIVIDEND-INTEREST) or interest on compensation (OS-COMPENSATION-INTEREST). TY 2026-27: Income-tax Act, 2025 s.93(1)(e) (p.142), s.94(1) (p.142). TY 2025-26: Income-tax Act, 1961 s.57(iii), s.58(1)(a) (thc p.310). Every regime. Which items it reaches is its condition on othersources.kind: the interest kinds, family pension and the kinds charged in full — not dividends, unit income, interest on compensation or the kinds whose entire amount is deducted, and not the kinds refused as unbuilt (D-202, D-193) (D-320). Nothing is deducted against a dividend deemed by S2 s.2(40)(f) / 1961 s.2(22)(f), so this row does not reach DEEMED_DIVIDEND: TY 2025-26, Income-tax Act, 1961 s.57 second proviso, ins. by the Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024 s.24(c) w.e.f. 1-10-2024 (egazette 2024/256436 p.24): \"no deduction shall be allowed in case of dividend income of the nature referred to in sub-clause (f) of clause (22) of section 2\"; TY 2026-27, Income-tax Act, 2025 s.93(2) as substituted by the Finance Act, 2026 s.44(b) (p.43): no deduction against any dividend income (the former row OS-DEEMED-DIVIDEND's statement, D-323).",
